{"availability":"available","full":"sebastianspicker/auto-pi-lot","name":"auto-pi-lot","description":"Graph mode for the Pi coding agent: plans tasks as validated graphs, runs them through a pure, replayable state machine, and only trusts results the host has checked.","category":"Productivity","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T19:42:39Z","updated":"2026-10-08T11:20:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sebastianspicker.github.io/auto-pi-lot/","topics":["agent-orchestration","ai-agents","coding-agent","dag","deterministic","event-sourcing","github-pages","llm","nodejs","orchestration","pi-agent","pi-coding-agent","state-machine","task-graph","typescript"],"demo":"https://sebastianspicker.github.io/auto-pi-lot/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:02.192Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:02.192Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:02.192Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:26:02.192Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Agents propose work; the harness accepts it from recorded evidence. Each task gets its own session, acceptance criteria, tool and token limits, deadline, and bounded retries. Checks run as actual processes. Optional reviewer tasks judge the producer's criteria. Failed checks and reviews feed evidence back into the next attempt.","This is an experimental local tool for trusted repositories. It edits your checkout in place and uses your model credentials. It does not commit, push, or deploy your work. Worktrees, a process sandbox, run-wide spending caps, nested plans, and a background supervisor are not implemented. No claim is made that this outperforms a single coding session."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastianspicker/auto-pi-lot/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e85a10b1382aba2753c33b8fb62607b6dfa942715fee08d5098623262965b4cf","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:02.334Z"},"overvie